{
  "$comment": "Frozen access-control scenarios. Each case fixes the attacker's move in advance and states what must not happen. Controls (category 'control') are the other half: a set that only proves refusals would be satisfied by a system that refuses everything. The model in these cases is scripted, so a prompt_injection case does not ask whether a model would obey injected text - it assumes the worst and scripts the model into obeying, then checks that obeying changes nothing. Changing a case changes what a score means, so edits belong in a version bump, not in a fix.",
